From c0f2a939b446809f0a05fc2fbaf492cbdd24dba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:46:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] MP4: limit atoms in nested containers (#1392)

Nested MP4 containers did not enforce the atom count limit applied at
the root level. A small file with many child atoms could consume
disproportionate memory while building the atom tree.

Apply the per-level limit to container children and reject files that
exceed it.

From 5f869755c8b6bc2dcdd36a11323ae45d3a851913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:25:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bound recursive Matroska and MP4 element trees (#1425)

The Matroska and MP4 parsers limited child elements per container, but
allowed that limit to repeat at every nesting level. A crafted media file
could therefore retain millions of small elements and exhaust process
memory while it was opened.

Carry a shared element count through recursive parsing so the existing
per-container limits also have a global bound.

From a6aff0bfce15975b065145f13a3020ccf5f5e5a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
