Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 14:44:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix writing too many offsets when updating MP4 stco/co64
 atoms (#1332)

This will fix a DoS with a crafted MP4 file causing too many offsets
to be written when updating the stco or co64 tables in MP4 files.

Credits for the discovery of this bug go to Yuen Ying Ng (Ruth)
(Cyber Security Researcher at PwC Hong Kong).

From fd97c86bcb924bd23e4c99bd25ffdf85f3a162b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 10:47:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] MP4: reject undersized table atoms (#1390)

MP4 chapter parsing subtracted table headers from atom lengths without
checking that the headers were present. A short atom could wrap the
read length and allocate the remainder of a large file.

Validate table sizes before reading their payloads and before updating
chunk offsets while saving.

